# saphira-bridge runtime identity: user saphira-bridge UID 149,
# primary group saphira-bridge GID 149.
#
# The bridge opens its packet sockets before dropping, because promiscuous mode
# needs CAP_NET_ADMIN, and it retains no capability afterwards: the sockets are
# established, and the daemon then writes nothing but its own log. A reload
# that would need a new socket is refused rather than attempted, so the daemon
# never needs the privilege back.
#
# 149 is allocated in package-name order from 147, the first free ID above the
# highest claimed identity (146 openldap), clear of systemd's block
# (127-131, 144, 145). It is NOT the 128 this fragment originally declared:
# 128 is systemd-resolve's, one package owns each declared identity, and
# saphira-bridge has never been published, so the move costs no migration and
# needs no legacy sidecar. Home /var/empty is shared infrastructure, left
# untouched by design.
#
# NOTE for operators: because the bridge runs as this user, any configuration
# directory it must read has to be readable by it. The package installs
# /etc/saphira as 0750 root:root, so a private copy for this daemon needs the
# group set to match, or the bridge must be pointed at a file it can read.
user saphira-bridge 149 saphira-bridge /var/empty /sbin/nologin
group saphira-bridge 149
